The total number of balls stays $12$ (two out, two in). All one colour means $(12, 0, 0)$ in some order, so $G - Y$ would be $12$, $0$ or $-12$ — a multiple of $3$.

Track $G - Y$:
- green + yellow → two red: $(g - 1) - (y - 1) = g - y$;
- green + red → two yellow: $(g - 1) - (y + 2) = g - y - 3$;
- yellow + red → two green: $(g + 2) - (y - 1) = g - y + 3$.

So $G - Y$ only changes by multiples of $3$. It starts at $3 - 4 = -1$, which is not a multiple of $3$, so it never becomes one. Hence the balls can never all be the same colour. ∎
